---
import Case from '../../layouts/Case.astro';
import Plate from '../../components/Plate.astro';
import Activity from '../../components/Activity.astro';
import activity from '../../data/cases/ulah-activity.json';
---

<Case
  title="Ulah"
  summary="A marketing site and a 55-project portfolio for a commercial architecture studio, taken from a Figma file to a live site on the client's existing hosting."
  facts={[
    { label: 'Client', value: 'Ulah, commercial architecture & design' },
    { label: 'My role', value: 'Front-end build, content pipeline, deployment' },
    { label: 'Timeline', value: 'Mar – Sep 2026' },
    { label: 'Stack', value: 'Astro, CSS, sharp, Tally' },
    { label: 'Status', value: 'Live' },
  ]}
  links={[{ label: 'Visit ulahdesign.com.br', href: 'https://ulahdesign.com.br' }]}
>
  <section class="case-section" aria-labelledby="brief">
    <h2 id="brief">The brief</h2>
    <div class="case-body">
      <p>
        Ulah is a commercial architecture studio, and it's run by my wife. They had a finished
        design in Figma and years of project photography, and needed a site that looks as
        considered as the stores they design.
      </p>
      <p>
        My background is backend and platform work, so this project was where I sharpened my
        front-end craft. I paired with <strong>Claude Code</strong> throughout, using it to iterate on
        layout and responsive detail against the Figma file, while I owned the structure, the
        content pipeline and every call on what shipped.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="case-section" aria-labelledby="work">
    <h2 id="work">What I built</h2>
    <ol class="decisions">
      <li>
        <h3>A faithful, responsive build of the Figma design</h3>
        <p>
          The homepage, the "about" and process sections and five portfolio pages match the design
          at desktop and phone widths, with the studio's own typeface (Neurial Grotesk) self-hosted and
          the design's SVG ornaments sized to spec.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>A photo pipeline instead of hand-exported images</h3>
        <p>
          The studio's photo folders mix camera RAW (CR3), HEIC and PNG. One script turns them into
          web-ready masters, auto-oriented with metadata stripped, and Astro generates the responsive
          sizes at build. Adding a project means dropping in a folder and re-running it.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>A portfolio the studio can reorder</h3>
        <p>
          The order of projects and of their photos lives in one YAML file. The first four photos of each
          project show up front and the rest open on demand, so long galleries stay fast.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Fits the hosting they already pay for</h3>
        <p>
          The site is fully static. A configurable base path let the new version be staged next to the
          old one on the same shared host before cutover, and a one-command deploy mirrors the build over
          FTPS. The first contact form was a PHP handler with reCAPTCHA; I replaced it with a Tally embed,
          leaving nothing server-side to maintain.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="case-section" aria-labelledby="plates">
    <h2 id="plates">The site</h2>
    <div class="plates plates--lead">
      <Plate
        number={1}
        src="/cases/ulah/home-desktop.webp"
        width={1440}
        height={900}
        alt="Ulah homepage at desktop width: a store interior photo behind the headline 'Projetos que desafiam o óbvio de forma estratégica' with two buttons."
        caption="Homepage, desktop. Captured from the live site, September 2026."
      />
      <Plate
        number={2}
        src="/cases/ulah/projetos.webp"
        width={1200}
        height={1667}
        alt="Ulah 'Lojas' portfolio page listing projects Baimas and Cia Coffee with four photos each."
        caption="Portfolio category page: each project shows four photos up front."
      />
      <Plate
        number={3}
        frame="phone"
        src="/cases/ulah/home-mobile.webp"
        width={390}
        height={844}
        alt="Ulah homepage on a phone-sized screen."
        caption="Homepage at phone width."
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="case-section" aria-labelledby="shipped">
    <h2 id="shipped">What shipped</h2>
    <div class="case-body">
      <ul class="shipped">
        <li>Live at <a href="https://ulahdesign.com.br">ulahdesign.com.br</a>: a homepage and <strong>five portfolio categories</strong>, from shops and kiosks to carts, homes and offices.</li>
        <li><strong>55 projects and 243 photos</strong>, all run through the photo pipeline.</li>
        <li>No server code to maintain: a static build and a one-command deploy.</li>
      </ul>
      <Activity data={activity} label="Commits per week" />
    </div>
  </section>
</Case>
